<title>USA: Phillips hopes to close Sweeny venture this yr.</title>
<headline>Phillips hopes to close Sweeny venture this yr.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Phillips Petroleum Co hopes to close a deal with Petroleos de Venezuela's Corpoven to build a coking unit at its Sweeny, Texas, refinery by the end of the year, chief executive Wayne Allen told a conference call after first quarter earnings.</p>
<p>Asked whether Phillips would contemplate any corporate acquisitions, Allen said any large deals were unlikely.</p>
<p>&quot;The industry has a lot of cash at the moment and does not have a terribly good record and larger deals tenbd to be very pricey, although we will be bidding on oil and gas properties,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
